{% comment %}
  Passthrough of Shopify's dynamic default crawl rules (robots.default_groups),
  kept in version control as a customization point for crawler-specific rules.

  robots.txt only controls crawling, not search-engine indexing — a page can
  still be indexed if discovered through an external link even when crawling
  is blocked here. To keep pages out of search results, this theme sets a
  sitewide `noindex` meta tag in snippets/meta-tags.liquid instead. Crawling
  stays open so link previews and future SEO tooling keep working.
{% endcomment %}
{%- for group in robots.default_groups -%}
  {{- group.user_agent }}

  {%- for rule in group.rules -%}
    {{ rule }}
  {%- endfor -%}

  {%- if group.sitemap != blank -%}
    {{ group.sitemap }}
  {%- endif -%}
{% endfor -%}
